==Maltese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|mt|ar|أَكَلَ}}. The expected basic form would be {{m|mt||*ekel}} or {{m|mt||*ikel}}. The initial vowel was lost by analogy with the forms of the 1st and 2nd persons. The remaining vowel was then lengthened by analogy with a hollow root. Such lengthening also occured in the imperative. Compare {{m|mt|ħa|t=to take}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kɪːl/|lang=mt}}
*: {{rhymes|ɪːl|lang=mt}}

===Verb===
{{mt-verb|jiekol|pp=mikul}}

# to [[eat]]
#: ''It-tifel qed '''jiekol''' issa.''
#:: The boy is eating now.

